// transfer_single_start -- operation model §3.2, group 1. The non-blocking
// half of transfer_single(). Present on every profile.
//
// completes_when: the channel is programmed and armed. NOT when the transfer
//                 has moved anything.
// waits for:      nothing. Straight-line stores; returns with the transfer
//                 running.
//
// Program, arm, return. The caller then polls check_completion() until it
// answers something other than PENDING -- or, on a target with blocking
// primitives, calls transfer_single(), which is exactly this plus the wait.
//
// The device knowledge is all here; the blocking layer adds only the loop.
// That is why a SystemVerilog regression that never calls this directly still
// tests it: transfer_single() is this function.
//
// THE CALLERS' OBLIGATIONS ARE UNCHANGED, and one of them gets sharper:
//
//   mode == HW_HANDSHAKE: the transfer cannot complete on its own. Something
//   must be calling request_chunk() on the matching wb_dma_hs_c concurrently
//   (§2.2). Splitting arm from wait does not help here -- the missing thing is
//   a second initiator, not a second thread.
//
//   cfg.auto_restart: the transfer has no completion event. CSR bit 11 sets
//   DONE only once ARS is clear, so nothing this function starts will ever make
//   check_completion() answer DONE. Someone must clear ARS (set_auto_restart(0))
//   or abort the channel (stop_channel_start()). In the blocking layer that is
//   a thread that never returns; HERE IT IS A LOOP THAT NEVER EXITS, which is a
//   firmware hang rather than a stalled PSS action. Same defect, less visible.
//
// Claims `inflight` FIRST, before touching a register. A start that would be
// the second on a live channel is reported without having corrupted the
// configuration of the first -- see wb_dma_ch_c.pss for what the guard is and
// is not.
import std_pkg::*;
import wb_dma_regs_pkg::*;
import wb_dma_types_pkg::*;

extend component wb_dma_ch_c {

    target function void transfer_single_start(wb_dma_ch_cfg_s cfg) {
        if (!inflight.try_put(1)) {
            message(NONE, "wb_dma: transfer_single_start() on a channel that already has an operation in progress");
            return;
        }

        configure_channel(cfg);

        // Arm. STILL A READ-MODIFY-WRITE: write_field is defined as one
        // (§21.14.1), so the configuration just written survives, and the
        // read still clears the ROC status bits -- harmless here because the
        // channel has not started yet. Nothing about the bus traffic changed;
        // only the spelling did.
        regs.csr.write_field("ch_en", 1);
    }
}
